4. Enhancement reciprocity

If you make an Enhancement, then within 30 days after first creating it you
must:

  a. make the complete corresponding source for that Enhancement publicly
     available under this license, including the files needed to build and
     modify it, except excluded secrets and Third-Party Materials; and
  b. submit a good-faith pull request to the Canonical source above containing
     the Enhancement.

The Canonical source's maintainers may accept, reject, or request changes to a
pull request. This condition requires submission; it does not require a
maintainer to merge the contribution. It applies to private Enhancements as
well as Enhancements made available to others.

